# Global-search item tap-through switches to section.moduleId, but items/details filters by the item's OWN module_id.
# 7 zone-1 items have item.module_id != store.module_id (mis-seeded). Search API (1027) groups them by store-module,
# so tap-through switches to the store-module and the detail 404s.
# Backend proof (item 60 "Chicken Drumsticks", store 7 HealthCare Pharmacy):
#   items/details/60 moduleId=1(grocery, item's real module) -> 200
#   items/details/60 moduleId=2 -> 404 ; moduleId=3(pharmacy, store/section module) -> 404
# App switched to pharmacy(3) -> details/60 -> 404 -> error UI "Something went wrong" + paired [FAIL] log (NOT silent).
# Suggested fix: guard should switch to the tapped PRODUCT's module_id (present in the /search/global payload), not section.moduleId.
